        "original_id": "c1a12aeb-2009-5428-b951-4b7a354a6c1e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Croydon Airport, Gatwick Airport, London, South London, south-east England, Central London, Crawley\n- Products: Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport\n- Systems: ICAO, IATA\n\nFacts:\n- Croydon Airport was an airport in South London, England, with ICAO code EGCR.\n- Croydon Airport was the main airport for London before it was replaced by Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport, and Gatwick Airport.\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, is a major international airport in south-east England, 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport has IATA code LGW and ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is the eighth-busiest airport in Europe.",
